// During the development process in Unity 3D, metadata files were automatically generated by the engine to manage and identify project assets and scripts. These .meta files contain important information such as unique identifiers (GUIDs), import settings, execution order, and asset references.

In this project, these files allowed Unity to correctly organize the scripts and maintain the connection between the game objects, scenes, and components used during the implementation of the prototype.

For example, the metadata configuration included information related to script import settings, execution priority, and asset management, which helped ensure proper integration and stability of the project within the Unity environment.
